        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "2eed770eaf5e38a5ac36a9e7239c2745f461ec33",
            "parents": [
                "dc498d4625f295270d1f5122732dbfde2c0b42ab"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/26/90126/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Unive Tien",
                "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "UniveTien"
            },
            "createdOn": 1778565386,
            "author": {
                "name": "Unive Tien",
                "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "UniveTien"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "Needs a concurrent-update guard.\n\nIf inotify and D-Bus paths are triggered simultaneously, processPackage and processStream both run against the same UpdateManager instance \u2014 clobbering shared state like parser, deviceUpdaterMap, activationProgress, etc.\n\nSuggest checking parser != nullptr (or an explicit updateInProgress flag) at the top of both functions and returning early if an update is already underway."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Unive Tien",
                        "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "UniveTien"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we need to see another PR with a pldm recipe update with PACKAGECONFIG updated so that the current defaults are kept so we don't have behavioral changes when building with yocto."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Unive Tien",
                        "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "UniveTien"
                    },
                    "message": "The option seems to be disabled by default already."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 132,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "I understand the intent to support both paths coexisting, but I don't think flipping the default to enabled is the right approach here.\n\nChanging the default silently activates inotify for all builds that don't explicitly set the option \u2014 consumers pick up a behavioral change without opting into it. That's especially problematic for platforms that lack the watched directory or that relied on the D-Bus-only path.\n\nI'd suggest leaving the default as disabled and letting callers opt in explicitly. That keeps it a conscious per-platform decision rather than something imposed on everyone."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 132,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> That keeps it a conscious per-platform decision rather than something imposed on everyone.\n\nAgree, but we can address that by making disabled the default in the pldm recipe.  The defaults here should really only apply to the CI environment where we want as much code enabled and exercised as possible."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 132,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Unive Tien",
                        "email": "unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "UniveTien"
                    },
                    "message": "The option seems to be disabled by default already in the recipe, since the `fw-update-pkg-inotify` was not appended."
                }
            ],
